    "summary": "The series bench (#234 against `1cc4412`, the last commit before spec 35) found the tick 3.4% faster but the rout 52% slower: 60.9 \u2192 92.4 ms a tick at 4,096 a side, 10 ticks. Spec 35 had moved the fleeing entries into the store, and the rout read and wrote them with `columns.value`/`put`. On the native store each is a GDScript method call into the field, about 1 \u00b5s, and there were roughly 8,700 a tick at 1,024 a side. Before, they were dictionary reads costing a few hundredths of a microsecond.",
